course: dictionary
lesson: 9515
title: Stiff: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so read the sentence around the word to find the right one. «Her new school shoes felt stiff and pinched her toes.» Here stiff means hard and not easy to bend, because new shoes are firm.
explain: When stiff describes a body, it means the muscles or joints are sore and hard to move. «After the hockey match, Sam woke with a stiff neck.» The word tells you his neck is hard to move, and the sore, tired feeling of the match fits that meaning.
explain: Stiff can also describe a person's manner: too formal, not warm or relaxed. «The stiff greeting from the new headteacher made everyone quiet.» Swap in «friendly» and the sentence stops making sense, so this is not the meaning here.
fact: Stiff means hard and not easy to bend or move.
fact: «Stiffer knees» means knees that are harder to bend, as people get older.
fact: Stiff can mean difficult or strong, as in «a stiff breeze» or «stiff competition».
fact: «Stiff» behaviour is too formal and not friendly or relaxed.
fact: «Bored stiff» and «scared stiff» mean very bored or very scared.
exercise: «Falling onto one straight, stiff arm often breaks the wrist.» What does stiff mean here? | *Hard and not easy to bend | Very bored | Soft and floppy | Friendly and relaxed
exercise: Which phrase means very bored? | a stiff neck | stiff competition | a stiff breeze | *bored stiff
exercise: «The stiff breeze made the kites dive.» What does stiff mean here? | Friendly | Warm | Soft | *Strong
test: «After the long run, my legs felt stiff and sore.» What does stiff mean in this sentence? | Ready for bed | Very quick | *Hard to move, with muscles that hurt
test: «The stiff reply from the shopkeeper made me feel unwelcome.» What does stiff suggest about the reply? | Loud and funny | *Too formal and not friendly | Warm and cheerful
exam: «The Amazon giant water lily has leaves held up by stiff ribs underneath, strong enough to hold a small child.» What does stiff mean here? | Happy and bouncy | Pale and thin | Sticky and wet | *Hard and firm, not easy to bend
